# NOTICE

## Upstream project

This repository is a **fork of [xrip/cmp50hx-unlock](https://github.com/xrip/cmp50hx-unlock)**.

That project is the origin of everything that makes the unlock possible: the
reverse-engineering of the SEC2 booter path and the FECS speed selectors, the
`610.43.03` driver patches (`patches/cmp50hx/`), the firmware extraction tooling
(`efi-unlock/extract_*.py`), the UEFI implementation (`efi-unlock/`,
`efi-unlock-windows/`), the register and fuse notes in `docs/`, the RT-core and
ReBAR work, and the original documentation, kept verbatim in
`docs/UPSTREAM-README.md` and `docs/UPSTREAM-README.RU.md`.

## What this fork adds

* `userspace-unlock/` — an independent userspace implementation of the same
  hardware sequence: vfio-pci in no-IOMMU mode for BAR0 and bus master,
  hugepage DMA buffers with physical addresses from `pagemap`, the FWSEC and
  SEC2 booter port loads, the WPR meta and radix-3 layout, plus the deployment
  tooling (`install.sh`, systemd unit, MOK helpers) and the diagnostics
  (`usplat`, `cmp50-regs`, `cmp50-fma`, `cmp50-dp4a`).
* `userspace-unlock/RESULTS.md`, `BIOS-SETUP.md`, `HANDOVER.md`, `FINISH-MOK.md`
  — the measurements, the negative results, and the board-level notes gathered
  while validating both paths on real hardware.
* `INSTALL.md` and the front-page `README.md`.

## What is deliberately not published

* `decompil/gsp_tu10x_610.43.03.elf.i64` — a 318 MB IDA database derived from
  NVIDIA firmware. It is a reverse-engineering artefact rather than something a
  user needs, it exceeds practical repository limits, and it is available from
  the upstream project. The analysis it supports is summarised in
  `docs/CMP50HX.md`.
* No credentials, host names or private addresses: the documents use `/opt/...`
  paths and `<host>` placeholders.

## Firmware and driver binaries

`efi-unlock/blobs/` contains NVIDIA firmware blobs (the SEC2 booter image, the
GSP firmware fragments, the board FWSEC) and `patches/` contains source patches
for the NVIDIA open kernel modules. They come from NVIDIA's own driver packages
and from the card's VBIOS, are redistributed here exactly as upstream
redistributes them, and remain subject to NVIDIA's licence terms. They are used
only to interoperate with hardware the user owns.

`efi-unlock-windows/tools/` contains prebuilt Windows executables from upstream;
their sources are next to them.

